            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic varices as a cause for pelvic pain: MRI appearance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>679-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pelvic venous congestion, as a cause of pelvic pain, is often overlooked. MR offers a noninvasive means of diagnosing this entity. Its appearance, as discussed, is important to recognize in patients who are referred for MR evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
